{"paragraphs":[{"text":"%md\n# About This Lab\n**Objective:** Become familiar with grouping and aggregating transformations\n**File locations:**\n**Successful outcome:**\n**Before you begin:**\n**Related lessons:** Working with DataFrames\n\nCopyright © 2010–2021 Cloudera. All rights reserved.\nNot to be reproduced or shared without prior written consent from Cloudera.\n\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:19:34-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorHide":true,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201821_856883528","id":"20171105-200834_1116095891","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:19:34-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:19:34-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"focus":true,"$$hashKey":"object:3483"},{"text":"%md\n## Overview\n\nIn this module we demonstrate how to summarize, group, and pivot data in a DataFrame.\n\n* Summarizing data with aggregate functions\n* Grouping data\n* Pivoting data","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:19:34-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201831_1119635417","id":"20210610-000856_746579081","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:19:34-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:19:34-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3484"},{"text":"%md\n# Setup\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:19:35-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201832_-1602918331","id":"20181114-164229_902436001","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:19:35-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:19:35-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3485"},{"title":"Read and persist the joined data","text":"%spark\n\n// Read the enhanced (joined) ride data from HDFS:\nval rides = spark.read.parquet(\"/duocar/joined/\")\n\n// Since we will be querying the `rides` DataFrame many times, let us persist it in memory to improve performance:\nrides.persist()\n","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:19:35-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201832_1101096599","id":"20210610-001349_2084269529","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:19:35-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:20:14-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3486"},{"text":"%md\n# Lesson\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:20:14-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201834_1708854367","id":"20210609-150445_381117564","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:20:15-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:20:15-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3487"},{"text":"%md\n## Summarizing data with aggregate functions\n\nSpark provides a number of summarization (aggregate) functions.  ","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:20:15-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201835_10782017","id":"20210610-001508_600148588","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:20:15-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:20:15-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3488"},{"title":"For example, the `describe` method provides basic summary statistics","text":"%spark\n\nrides.describe(\"distance\").show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:20:15-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201836_907361149","id":"20210610-001608_697670181","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:20:15-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:20:25-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3489"},{"title":"Use the `count`, `countDistinct`, and `approx_count_distinct` functions to compute various column counts","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{count, countDistinct, approx_count_distinct}\n\nrides.select(count(\"*\"), count(\"distance\"), countDistinct(\"distance\"), approx_count_distinct(\"distance\")).show()\n/*\n# ======================================================================================================================================================= #\n# Function\t                              ¿What does it count?                          Handlling of Nulls\t                 Accuracy / Performance       #\n# ======================================================================================================================================================= #\n# count(\"*\")\t                          Counts the total number of rows.              Includes rows even if they contain   Accurate and very fast.      # \n#                                                                                       null values in their columns.                                     # \n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n# count(\"column\")\t                      Counts the number of non-null                 Ignores null values.                 Accurate, but not as fast.   # \n#                                         values in a column.                                                                                             # \n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n# countDistinct(\"column\")\t              Counts the number of unique,                  Ignores null values.                 Accurate, but very slow and  # \n#                                         non-null values in a column.                                                       computationally expensive    #\n#                                                                                                                            for Big Data.                #\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n# approx_count_distinct(\"column\")\t      Provides an approximate estimate of the       Ignores null values.                 Approximate (default margin  #\n#                                         number of unique values using algorithms                                           of error ~5%),               #\n#                                         (such as HyperLogLog).                                                             but much faster.             #\n# ======================================================================================================================================================= #\n*/","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:20:25-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201836_413525881","id":"20210610-001750_2040367422","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:20:26-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:20:37-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3490"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\nThe `count` function returns the number of rows with non-null values.\nUse `count(lit(1))` rather than `count(1)` as an alternative to `count(\"*\")`.\n\n`count(1)` may fail in some versions of Spark because Spark expects a column, not a value.\n`count(lit(1))` creates a virtual column in which all rows have the constant value 1, and it always works.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:20:37-0800","config":{"tableHide":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201837_-1713932242","id":"20210610-001844_1194688367","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:20:38-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:20:38-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3491"},{"title":"The `agg` method returns the same results and can be applied to grouped data","text":"%spark\n\nrides.agg(count(\"*\"), count(\"distance\"), countDistinct(\"distance\"), approx_count_distinct(\"distance\")).show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:20:38-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201838_-582402451","id":"20210610-002029_229017827","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:20:38-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:20:47-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3492"},{"title":"Use the `sum` and `sumDistinct` functions to compute various column sums","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{sum, sumDistinct}\n\nrides.agg(sum(\"distance\"), sumDistinct(\"distance\")).show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:20:47-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201839_-2010553036","id":"20210610-002159_105666656","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:20:47-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:20:55-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3493"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\nWhen would one use the `sumDistinct` function?\n\nExamples of use:\n\n**Aggregations involving data duplication due to joins**:\nWhen joining two tables (for example, Sales and Customers), a row from the primary table may be multiplied due to multiple matches in the secondary table; using a standard `sum` would result in the amounts being duplicated.\n`sumDistinct` ensures that each original value is included in the sum exactly once.\n\n**Calculating totals for unique metrics**:\nFor instance, calculating the cumulative total of unique categorical or numerical values—such as the total number of distinct fixed rates applied.\n\n**Data integrity validation**:\nUsed to compare a grand total (`sum`) against the total of unique, non-repeated values (`sumDistinct`) in order to detect duplicates within massive datasets.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:20:55-0800","config":{"tableHide":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201847_-1769130369","id":"20210610-002251_287057366","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:20:56-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:20:56-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3494"},{"title":"Spark SQL provides a number of summary statistics","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{mean, stddev, variance, skewness, kurtosis}\n\nrides.agg(mean(\"distance\"), stddev(\"distance\"), variance(\"distance\"), skewness(\"distance\"), kurtosis(\"distance\")).show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:20:56-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201848_-1411172834","id":"20210610-002353_144721134","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:20:56-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:00-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3495"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\n`mean` is an alias for `avg`, `stddev` is an alias for the sample standard deviation `stddev_samp`, and `variance` is an alias for the sample variance `var_samp`.  \nThe population standard deviation and population variance are available via `stddev_pop` and `var_pop`, respectively.\n\n`mean(\"distance\")`     (**Mean**):               The average distance traveled.\n\n`stddev(\"distance\")`   (**Standard Deviation**): How much the data points differ, on average, from the mean.\n\n`variance(\"distance\")` (**Variance**):           A measure of dispersion (the square of the standard deviation).\n\n`skewness(\"distance\")` (**Skewness**):           Indicates whether the data is skewed to the right (positive values / unusually long trips) or to the left.\n\n`kurtosis(\"distance\")` (**Kurtosis**):           Measures how concentrated the data is around the mean, as well as the presence of extreme values (`outliers`).","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:00-0800","config":{"tableHide":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201849_1454150417","id":"20210610-002536_624409551","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:00-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:01-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3496"},{"title":"Use the `min` and `max` functions to compute the minimum and maximum, respectively","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{min,max}\n\nrides.agg(min(\"distance\"), max(\"distance\")).show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:01-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201850_2129699680","id":"20210610-004653_1846994497","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:01-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:03-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3497"},{"title":"Use the `first` and `last` functions to compute the first and last values, respectively","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{first,last}\n(rides\n  .orderBy(\"distance\")\n  .agg(first(\"distance\", false), last(\"distance\", false))\n  .show())","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:03-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201851_1183935374","id":"20210610-004917_1946337516","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:04-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:10-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3498"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\nNull values sort before valid numerical values.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:10-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201852_1210054121","id":"20210610-005028_192865414","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:10-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:10-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3499"},{"title":"Use the `corr`, `covar_samp`, or `covar_pop` functions to measure the linear association between two columns","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{corr, covar_samp, covar_pop}\n\n(rides \n  .agg(corr(\"distance\", \"duration\"), covar_samp(\"distance\", \"duration\"), covar_pop(\"distance\", \"duration\"))\n  .show())\n/*\n# ======================================================================================================================================================= #\n# Function                                ¿What does it calculate?                     Handling of Nulls (null)           Precision / Performance         #\n# ======================================================================================================================================================= #\n# corr(\"distance\", \"duration\")            Calculates the Pearson correlation           Ignores rows where either          Exact. Moderate cost; scales    #\n#                                         coefficient (-1 to 1). Measures the          of the 2 columns contains          variables to normalize the      #\n#                                         strength and direction of the linear         a null value.                      measurement of the              #\n#                                         relationship.                                                                   relationship.                   #\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n# covar_samp(\"distance\", \"duration\")      Calculates the sample covariance.            Ignores rows where either          Exact. Fast; divides by         #\n#                                         Measures whether both variables vary         of the 2 columns contains          (N - 1), thus requiring at      #\n#                                         together in the same direction.              a null value.                      least 2 valid rows.             #\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n# covar_pop(\"distance\", \"duration\")       Calculates the population covariance.        Ignores rows where either          Exact. Fast; divides by N       #\n#                                         Represents joint dispersion.                 of the 2 columns contains          (the total number of valid      #\n#                                                                                      a null value.                      processed in the group).        #\n# ======================================================================================================================================================= #\n*/","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:10-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201853_-1505038156","id":"20210610-005108_1053279348","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:10-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:12-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3500"},{"title":"The `collect_list` and `collect_set` functions return a column of array type","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{collect_list, collect_set}\n\nrides.agg(collect_list(\"service\")).show(true) // The list is so long (due to duplicate values)\n                                              // that setting truncate=True would cause the paragraph output to be cut off.\n\nrides.agg(collect_set(\"service\")).show(false)","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:12-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201857_296212017","id":"20210610-005214_1158162099","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:13-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:15-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3501"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\n`collect_list` does not remove duplicates and will return a very long array in this case.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:15-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201858_-123136687","id":"20210610-005311_924230397","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:15-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:15-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3502"},{"text":"%md\n## Grouping data","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:15-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201859_876922842","id":"20210610-005406_1475956556","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:15-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:15-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3503"},{"title":"Use the `agg` method with the `groupBy` (or `groupby`) method to refine your analysis","text":"%spark\n\n(rides \n  .groupBy(\"rider_student\")\n  .agg(count(\"*\"), count(\"distance\"), mean(\"distance\"), stddev(\"distance\"))\n  .show())","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:16-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201860_-2040326432","id":"20210610-005459_562960104","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:16-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:19-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3504"},{"title":"You can use more than one column in the `groupBy` method","text":"%spark\n\n(rides \n  .groupBy(\"rider_student\", \"service\")\n  .agg(count(\"*\"), count(\"distance\"), mean(\"distance\"), stddev(\"distance\"))\n  .orderBy(\"rider_student\", \"service\")\n  .show())","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:19-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201861_684189360","id":"20210610-005507_72302918","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:19-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:23-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3505"},{"title":"Use the `rollup` method to get some subtotals","text":"%spark\n\n(rides\n  .rollup(\"rider_student\", \"service\")\n  .agg(count(\"*\"), count(\"distance\"), mean(\"distance\"), stddev(\"distance\"))\n  .orderBy(\"rider_student\", \"service\")\n  .show())","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:24-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201862_1209879693","id":"20210610-005622_943449604","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:24-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:28-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3506"},{"title":" Use the `grouping` function to identify grouped rows","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{grouping}\n\n(rides\n  .rollup(\"rider_student\", \"service\")\n  .agg(grouping(\"rider_student\"), grouping(\"service\"), count(\"*\"), count(\"distance\"), mean(\"distance\"), stddev(\"distance\"))\n  .orderBy(\"rider_student\", \"service\")\n  .show())","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:28-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201863_-172646690","id":"20210610-005654_256119548","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:28-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:31-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3507"},{"title":"Use the `cube` method to get all subtotals","text":"%spark\n\n(rides\n  .cube(\"rider_student\", \"service\")\n  .agg(count(\"*\"), count(\"distance\"), mean(\"distance\"), stddev(\"distance\"))\n  .orderBy(\"rider_student\", \"service\")\n  .show())","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:31-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201864_-221029013","id":"20210610-005725_963905302","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:32-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:35-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3508"},{"title":"Use the `grouping_id` function to identify grouped rows","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{grouping_id}\n\n(rides\n  .cube(\"rider_student\", \"service\")\n  .agg(grouping_id(\"rider_student\", \"service\"), count(\"*\"), count(\"distance\"), mean(\"distance\"), stddev(\"distance\"))\n  .orderBy(\"rider_student\", \"service\")\n  .show())","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:35-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201865_-1893053836","id":"20210610-005451_1732153318","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:35-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:38-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3509"},{"text":"%md\n## Pivoting data","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:38-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201866_-1553063393","id":"20210610-005420_612603285","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:38-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:38-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3510"},{"title":"The following use case is common","text":"%spark\n\nrides.groupBy(\"rider_student\", \"service\").count().orderBy(\"rider_student\", \"service\").show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:38-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201867_-1899894233","id":"20210610-005933_221072209","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:39-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:41-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3511"},{"title":"We can also use the `pivot` method to produce a cross-tabulation","text":"%spark\n\nrides.groupBy(\"rider_student\").pivot(\"service\").count().show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:41-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201899_-1846681426","id":"20210610-010054_1613521590","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:41-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:46-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3512"},{"title":" We can also perform other aggregations","text":"%spark\n\nrides.groupBy(\"rider_student\").pivot(\"service\").mean(\"distance\").show()\nrides.groupBy(\"rider_student\").pivot(\"service\").agg(mean(\"distance\")).show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:46-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201900_1870396119","id":"20210610-010132_1478700646","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:47-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:21:55-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3513"},{"title":"You can explicitly choose the values that are pivoted to columns","text":"%spark\n\nrides.groupBy(\"rider_student\").pivot(\"service\", Array(\"Car\", \"Grand\")).agg(mean(\"distance\")).show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:21:55-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201901_706831373","id":"20210610-010326_792064606","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:21:55-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:22:02-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3514"},{"title":"Additional aggregation functions produce additional columns","text":"%spark\n\nrides.groupBy(\"rider_student\").pivot(\"service\", Array(\"Car\")).agg(count(\"distance\"), mean(\"distance\")).show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:22:02-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201903_-1656899683","id":"20210610-005930_840992557","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:22:02-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:22:06-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3515"},{"text":"%md\n# Lab\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:22:07-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201903_1919183304","id":"20210609-150527_79851234","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:22:07-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:22:07-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3516"},{"title":"1 - Who are DuoCar's top 10 riders in terms of number of rides taken?","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{col}\n\n(rides\n  .filter(col(\"cancelled\") === false)\n  .groupBy(\"rider_id\")\n  .count()\n  .orderBy(col(\"count\").desc)\n  .show(10))","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:22:07-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201904_-1499579691","id":"20210610-011625_1452114877","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:22:07-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:22:11-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3517"},{"title":"2 - Who are DuoCar's top 10 drivers in terms of total distance driven?","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{sum}\n\n(rides\n  .groupBy(\"driver_id\")\n  .agg(sum(\"distance\").alias(\"sum_distance\"))\n  .orderBy(col(\"sum_distance\").desc)\n  .show(10))","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:22:11-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201905_86251166","id":"20210610-011614_1512222076","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:22:11-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:22:14-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3518"},{"title":"3 - Compute the distribution of cancelled rides","text":"%spark\n\nrides.groupBy(\"cancelled\").count.show","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:22:14-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201918_726120113","id":"20210610-011606_391730360","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:22:15-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:22:18-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3519"},{"title":"4 - Compute the distribution of ride star rating. When is the ride star rating missing?","text":"%spark\n\nrides.groupBy(\"star_rating\").count().orderBy(\"star_rating\").show()\n\n// The star rating is missing when a ride is cancelled:\nrides.groupBy(\"star_rating\").pivot(\"cancelled\").count().orderBy(\"star_rating\").show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:22:18-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795015201919_1050101866","id":"20210610-011552_1782016420","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T07:20:01-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:22:18-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:22:23-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:3520"},{"title":"5 - Compute the average star rating for each level of car service. Is the star rating correlated with the level of car service?","text":"%spark\n\nrides.groupBy(\"service\").mean(\"star_rating\").show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:22:23-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"editorHide":false,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":